WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.401
You're back exclusively with

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.236
New York Congressman Hakeem Jeffries,

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:03.937
who is running

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.605
unopposed to become the leader

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.640
of the Democrats in the House.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.175
Congressman, thanks so much

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.210
for staying with us.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.544
What is your relationship

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.380
like with your Republican counterpart,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.180
Kevin McCarthy,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.515
who wants to be the speaker?

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.683
When was the last time

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.351
you spoke with him?

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.055
I haven't had a conversation

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.758
with Leader McCarthy Carthy recently.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:25.825
I do have,

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.128
I think, a much warmer relationship

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.229
with Steve Scalise.

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.864
Look forward to working

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.232
whenever and wherever possible.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:32.866
However, Jake,

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.534
with the entire House

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.668
Republican Conference

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.137
and the leadership team

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.438
to find common ground

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:39.572
to get things done

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.608
for everyday Americans to make progress.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.611
But of course, we will fiercely

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:45.678
and vigorously

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.447
oppose any attempts

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.682
at Republican overreach

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.018
and any Republican extremism.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.120
And I'm hopeful

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.456
that the Republican leadership

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.258
will take lessons away

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.126
from the rejection of extremism

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.494
by the American people

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.762
all across the land

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.198
and not double and triple down on it

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.933
in the next Congress.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.034
Do you think he's fit

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.102
to be the next leader,

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:09.803
Kevin McCarthy,

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:10.937
the next leader of the Republicans?

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.139
You've had some harsh words for him

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:13.973
saying it's impossible

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:14.941
to take him seriously.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:15.875
And when people ask you about

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.409
Kevin McCarthy,

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.310
you say, Kevin,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.878
who do you think he's fit

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.746
to be speaker of the House?

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:22.982
Well, that's

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:23.883
a decision ultimately

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.085
that the House Republican Conference

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.252
is going to have to make.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.420
He does seem to be struggling

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.655
to get the two way team.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.957
Let's see what happens on January 3rd.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.559
There is going to be

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:36.362
because of the narrow majority that House

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.431
Republicans are going to have,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:38.898
the far

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.399
right wing,

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.302
the MAGA caucus is going to be empowered

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.069
and emboldened.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.437
It's going to make it tougher

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.206
for McCarthy to govern as speaker

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.308
if he does, in fact, become speaker.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:50.777
If Kevin McCarthy needs votes to pass

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.645
essential legislation

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.280
such as keeping the government open

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.149
or raising the debt limit.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:58.451
Will Democrats be willing to help him

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.787
if the Freedom Caucus folks the Marjorie

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.589
Taylor Greens of the world

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.058
refuse to participate

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:07.927
Well, it seems to me

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.395
that that's a case by case basis.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.564
But Democrats have always been willing

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.899
to lean in on making sure

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.767
that we fully fund the government.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.568
And Democrats

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.337
have always been willing to lean in

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:17.971
and making sure

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:19.072
that we meet

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:19.839
our nation's

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:22.442
obligations and do not default

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.710
on our debt.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.512
For the first time in American history,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:26.880
I think it's also important

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.148
to point out, Jake,

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.450
that we have consistently

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.885
fought against extremism

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.553
on the Republican side,

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:36.456
including when it manifested itself often

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.993
during the former president's tenure,

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.928
while at the same time

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.097
being able to find common ground

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.099
to make progress for the American people.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.800
We did it with criminal justice reform.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.636
I was delighted to be involved

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.670
personally

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.172
in trying to negotiate a historic

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.907
criminal justice reform

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:55.108
with the Trump administration

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.910
and working with my colleague,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.778
former Republican Congressman

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:00.780
Doug Collins from Georgia.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.183
Certainly, Speaker Pelosi led the effort

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.250
to make sure

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.718
that we could arrive at an agreement

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:06.452
around the U.S.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.687
Mexico-Canada

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.557
trade agreement, reform, the new NAFTA

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:11.391
in a way

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.493
that benefited working families

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.361
organized labor

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.563
and people from the heartland

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.097
and throughout the country.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:18.898
And we consistently

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:19.966
have found common ground,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.000
even with some of the most

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.802
recent legislative victories

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.137
during this current Congress.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.471
I hope that that's a record

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.774
that we can build upon moving forward.

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.342
House Republicans announced this week

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.610
their oversight plans,

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:31.211
which include

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.378
taking a look at the withdrawal

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.413
from Afghanistan,

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.948
the origins of COVID,

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:37.150
the FBI search at Mar a Lago.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.018
I can see that there could be

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.353
theoretically legitimate

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:41.487
oversight questions

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:42.689
on each of those topics

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:43.890
that could be asked

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.524
Will House

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.825
Democrats participate

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.594
in these investigations in good faith?

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.229
Or do you see it as your role

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.264
to defend the Biden administration?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.635
Well, we will absolutely

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.470
defend the Biden administration

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:59.539
and his track record of success

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:02.275
if it comes under assault

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:05.144
by people attempting to politicize

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.780
our governmental responsibilities,

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.582
without question.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.718
And I expect that we will strongly

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.353
and vigorously

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.187
be involved

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:17.190
in pushing back against any effort

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:20.493
at overreach by the extreme MAGA

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.562
Republican wing of the House

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.230
Republican Conference.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:27.033
At the same time, we're going to continue

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:27.400
to try

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.403
to find common ground legislatively

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:31.904
whenever possible

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:35.141
I think that the time for politics ends

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.810
in the immediate aftermath of a campaign,

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:40.380
and it has to be some space to govern.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:40.713
That's what

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:41.814
the American people

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.016
Democrats, Republicans,

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.018
independents, people in the North,

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.286
the South, the East, the West,

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.354
the Midwest want to see happen.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:49.722
Democrats are willing

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.658
to lean into that regard.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.092
I'm hopeful

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.260
that my Republican colleagues

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.495
will join us.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.930
Lastly, sir, Elon Musk reinstated

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.600
Donald Trump to Twitter yesterday

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.403
just to remind folks at home

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.171
Trump wasn't banned for mean tweets.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:05.672
He was banned

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.906
because he used the platform

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.875
to incite a violent insurrection

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:09.942
on the Capitol.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.210
What's your reaction to Trump

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.512
being reinstated on Twitter?

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:16.849
You know, I have no

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:17.850
reaction at this point

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.217
in time

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.053
to anything that Elon Musk

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.788
or Donald Trump

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:23.056
does, particularly

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:25.024
as it relates to social media.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:25.925
I am going to continue

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.561
to try to lean into the principles

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:29.929
of equal protection

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:30.463
under the law,

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.932
liberty and justice for all government

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.300
of the people by the people

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.568
and for the people,

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.470
and build upon the amazing progress

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:37.970
that House

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:38.604
Democrats

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:40.273
have brought to bear in partnership

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.174
with Senate

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:43.209
Democrats and President Biden

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:46.179
and continue to push for

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:48.648
American exceptionalism

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:50.483
throughout the country.

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:50.783
All right,

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:52.352
Congressman Hakeem Jeffries,

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.453
Democrat of New York,

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.154
and likely the next

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.756
leader of House Democrats.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.025
It would be a historic moment.

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:00.626
Congressman, congratulations

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:01.060
ahead of time.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.062
Thanks for joining us today.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:05.231
Thank you, Jake.

